  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When rotating a station (locally), the nameplate of the user inside always stays above the chair position as if it wasn't rotated instead of being above the avatar head, causing the nameplate to fly around weirdly (and literally in your face) when the chair is rotated e.g. in a vehicle in which your are in as well. \n\nIt's position should instead rotate with the station as if it was parented to it. If this is too complex for VRChat to handle, a station needs to expose a bool (to parent the nameplate of the user inside to that chair if needed) which we can manipulate at runtime (both in SDK2 and SDK3), else multi-chair vehicles will keep having this issue and their usage is disturbed with nameplates being on.",
